July this year was the hottest month in France since records began in 1900, according to meteorologists. It was also France's third-driest July, with rainfall nearly 70 percent below average. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e5c8712-8f85-11f1-ae44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-03T140809Z-1054843999-RC22RMATIOH6-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e5c8712-8f85-11f1-ae44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-03T140809Z-1054843999-RC22RMATIOH6-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b2a1ebe-90a5-11f1-858d-076e9a7b708c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 14:30:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3e5c8712-8f85-11f1-ae44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-03T140809Z-1054843999-RC22RMATIOH6-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">REUTERS - Yves Herman</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ile-de-France region files suit for compensation over Fontainebleau forest fire</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260805-ile-de-france-region-files-suit-for-compensation-over-fontainebleau-forest-fire</link><description>
The Ile-de-France regional council this week launched a civil law suit over the recent wildfire which decimated more than 2,000 hectares of the Fontainebleau forest, south of Paris. A criminal investigation has been opened into the blaze, which the national forestry office says caused significant environmental damage. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1852b46a-81b1-11f1-9997-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26195425873893.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1852b46a-81b1-11f1-9997-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26195425873893.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fd7b74a-90b2-11f1-8e75-e52d3b665f72</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 13:36:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1852b46a-81b1-11f1-9997-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26195425873893.jpg">© Emma Da Silva / AP</source><dc:creator>Ollia Horton with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France welcomes Algeria’s arrest of alleged DZ Mafia crime boss</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260805-france-welcomes-algeria-s-arrest-of-alleged-dz-mafia-crime-boss</link><description>
France's Minister of Justice, Gérald Darmanin has hailed Algerian security services for their work in the arrest of an alleged key figure in Marseille's crime world.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b9eb3a88-60e4-11f1-820c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-05T072936Z-1032450962-RC2B0IAD7AAM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-CRIME.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b9eb3a88-60e4-11f1-820c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-05T072936Z-1032450962-RC2B0IAD7AAM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-CRIME.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5dee52f6-90b9-11f1-af78-290a92cb9c17</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:14:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b9eb3a88-60e4-11f1-820c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-05T072936Z-1032450962-RC2B0IAD7AAM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-CRIME.jpg">REUTERS - Manon Cruz</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French wildfires expose cache of buried Second World War shells</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-french-wildfires-expose-buried-wwii-shells-gironde-bordeaux</link><description>
